From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:26:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/43] Shaders: a sampler chosen by control flow between two
 immediate samplers

The title's programs pick an address mode by control flow: one of two
immediate samplers, set in SGPRs on each side of a branch, reaches the
sample through a phi. `descriptor_phi` takes heap-index sources only, so
these programs stopped with "a descriptor chosen by control flow" (37 pixel
and 3 mesh programs of the retail pack).

A handle cannot be chosen by control flow (the validator: "Resource handle
should returned by createHandle"), and a shader sampler range cannot span
two static samplers (D3D12 refuses the pipeline). So the sample is made
through each of the two static samplers and each result channel picked by a
bit made at the join. A phi of one immediate sampler is that sampler.

- lower: `immediate_sampler_pair` gives the two handles and the bit;
  `image` emits the sample op once more through the second handle
  (`Module::call_with`) and selects per channel; `calculateLOD` likewise.
- bitcode: `Module::call_with`, a copy of a call with one argument replaced.
- A draw test: a branch on a root constant picks a wrapping or a clamping
  point sampler for a sample at u = 1.25 of a red and a green texel; the
  draw reads the texel of the chosen one, on hardware and WARP.

(cherry picked from commit 77f83f9819d40030e13bd1ccd4024ff04db24528)
